.nf
YASMV manual                                                 explain-step

.ti 0
SYNOPSIS

.in 3
explain-step [-at <index>] [-c <expression>] [-minimize] [options]

.ti 0
DESCRIPTION

.fi
.in 3
Explain why the selected native trace cannot continue by one transition
under the supplied assumptions. Requires a loaded model and a current trace.

-at K preserves states 0 through K, including the action at K. Indices start
at zero. Omitting -at uses the complete current trace. The parent is replayed
before analysis; the current native trace is preserved.

-minimize requests minimization of the inconsistent constraint set. Evidence
records whether minimization completed. Satisfiable requests have no
inconsistency to explain.

-c <expression> adds an assumption (repeatable). -wall-ms <N> limits computation
time; -conflicts <N> and -propagations <N> limit solver work. -async submits a
background job. Use job wait to retrieve its result or job cancel to cancel it.
Ctrl-C cancels a waiting job. job show -full displays complete evidence.
Shell options use one dash; -- starts an SMV comment.

.ti 0
EXAMPLES

.nf
.in 3
>> explain-step -at 0 -c action = ACK -minimize
>> job show -full

.ti 0
SEE ALSO

.fi
.in 3
help job, help reach, help simulate, help workspace.
